{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "behavioral-patterns-collection",
		"name": "Behavioral Design Patterns - E-commerce Order System",
		"description": "This collection demonstrates the implementation of 4 behavioral design patterns:\n\n1. **Chain of Responsibility**: Order validation through handlers\n2. **Command**: PlaceOrderCommand with undo functionality\n3. **Observer**: NotificationService with EmailNotification and SMSNotification\n4. **Strategy**: Different payment strategies (CreditCard, PayPal, etc.)\n\nThe system follows Spring Boot layered architecture with H2 database persistence.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Create Order",
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"exec": [
							"if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 201) {",
							"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
							"    if (jsonData.id) {",
							"        pm.environment.set(\"orderId\", jsonData.id);",
							"    }",
							"}"
						],
						"type": "text/javascript"
					}
				}
			],
			"request": {
				"method": "POST",
				"header": [
					{
						"key": "Content-Type",
						"value": "application/json"
					}
				],
				"body": {
					"mode": "raw",
					"raw": "{\n  \"customerName\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"totalAmount\": 999.99,\n  \"paymentMethod\": \"CREDIT_CARD\"\n}"
				},
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders",
					"host": [
						"{{baseUrl}}"
					],
					"path": [
						"orders"
					]
				},
				"description": "**Design Patterns Used:**\n- **Command Pattern**: PlaceOrderCommand encapsulates the order placement request\n- **Chain of Responsibility**: Order goes through validation chain (InventoryCheckHandler -> PaymentValidationHandler)\n- **Observer Pattern**: NotificationService observers are notified when order is placed\n- **Strategy Pattern**: Payment method is selected based on the paymentMethod field\n\nThis endpoint validates the order and creates it in the H2 database."
			},
